            "text": "The top global news headlines for today, July 28, 2026, are led by a major natural disaster in Japan and critical diplomatic meetings at the White House:\n\n### 1. Magnitude 7.1 Earthquake Striking Southern Japan\nA powerful 7.1-magnitude earthquake struck Kumamoto Prefecture on Japan's southern island of Kyushu. The earthquake caused severe structural damage, highlighted by the collapse and a reported gas explosion at the Aeon Mall in Kashima Town, which trapped multiple shoppers and employees, resulting in several confirmed deaths and dozens of injuries. The disaster also caused blackouts, cracked roads, and derailed a train at Yatsushiro station. While a tsunami advisory was briefly issued for the Ariake and Yatsushiro Seas, it was lifted within two hours. \n* **Source:** [PBS News](https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/7-1-magnitude-earthquake-rattles-japan-but-tsunami-advisory-is-lifted)\n\n### 2. Trump Hosts Back-to-Back Meetings with Zelenskyy and Netanyahu\nIn Washington, President Donald Trump held highly anticipated, consecutive meetings in the Oval Office with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy and Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. \n* **Zelenskyy Meeting:** Zelenskyy, who was in Washington to attend the funeral of the late Senator Lindsey Graham, characterized his sit-down with Trump as a \"good meeting.\" They discussed strategic cooperation, diplomacy, and securing production licenses for Patriot air defense interceptor missiles.\n* **Netanyahu Meeting:** Tensions remained high as Netanyahu sought to mend his relationship with Trump. Their talks occurred amidst disagreements over military campaigns in the Middle East and Trump's recent diplomatic overtures toward Tehran.\n* **Source:** [The Guardian](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2026/jul/28/trump-hosts-back-to-back-meetings-with-zelenskyy-and-netanyahu)",
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
